.Dd March 3, 2025
.Dt SIGMA-SH 1
.Os SigmaOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm sigma-sh
.Nd Sovereign POSIX and zero-trust interactive command shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar command
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl s
.Op Ar script_file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is the primary sovereign command language interpreter for
.Dx SigmaOS .
It executes commands read from standard input, specified strings, or script files.
.Pp
.Nm
features built-in post-quantum cryptographic security enforcement, process isolation
via OpenBSD-style pledge and unveil sandboxing, and direct integration with
the SigmaOS kernel microservice IPC layer.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl c Ar command
Read and execute commands from the string
.Ar command .
.It Fl i
Force interactive shell execution with prompt printing and line editing.
.It Fl s
Read commands from standard input.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SIGMA_PATH"
.It Ev PATH
Search path for executable binaries, defaults to
.Pa /system/bin:/usr/bin .
.It Ev SIGMA_PLEDGE
Default pledge sandbox restrictions enforced on child processes spawned by
.Nm .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.sigmashrc"
.It Pa /etc/sigmashrc
System-wide shell initialization configuration file.
.It Pa ~/.sigmashrc
User-specific shell configuration file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sigma-pkg 8 ,
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr pledge 2
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility was created for the
.Dx SigmaOS
Sovereign Operating System project.
